  "core_question": "How to design a defensible first version of an AI sepsis risk score clinical decision support tool for a 12‑hospital health system covering clinical safety, legal/regulatory exposure, and financial structure.",
  "rationale": "The project requires expertise in clinical validation and workflow integration (healthcare), regulatory classification and liability management (legal), and pricing, cost–benefit analysis, and subscription economics (finance).",
  "routes": ["healthcare", "legal", "finance"],
  "sub_questions": {
    "healthcare": "For a 12‑hospital health system deploying an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool via per‑seat annual subscriptions, what clinical safety measures—including data quality controls, model validation protocols, real‑time monitoring, workflow integration strategies, and post‑market surveillance plans—should be implemented to ensure patient safety and maintain clinician trust in the first version?",
    "legal": "Given a 12‑hospital health system rolling out an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool with per‑seat subscriptions, what legal and regulatory steps—including FDA device classification, HIPAA compliance, data governance, informed consent requirements, liability mitigation, state law considerations, and contract provisions—must be addressed to minimize exposure for the first version?",
    "finance": "For a 12‑hospital health system offering an AI sepsis risk score CDS tool on a per‑seat annual subscription model, what financial structure—including pricing strategy, cost allocation, revenue projections, ROI calculation, capital budgeting, and risk mitigation—should be designed to support a defensible first version?"
  },
  "requires_recency_disclosure": true,
  "recency_notes": "Potentially stale FDA AI/ML medical device guidance post‑2024, recent CMS reimbursement updates for CDS tools, and evolving state privacy laws."
}
